      // [src_vespucci_britannica, src_vespucci_dbi | 1500-1507 | reference article, Italian biographical dictionary] Britannica says that on his return to Spain in 1500 he prepared a new expedition toward the Indian Ocean and that the Spanish government did not welcome the proposal; the DBI documents that on 13 March 1505 the Casa's officers were ordered to organise an expedition under Vespucci and Vicente Yanez Pinzon, re-authorised in August 1506 and ended by the king's death in September, and Britannica adds that he helped prepare other expeditions without sailing again. The planning is documented; how far the initiative was his own, rather than royal orders, is less clear. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): reviewed and kept unchanged.
