      // [src_vespucci_britannica, src_vespucci_dbi, src_vespucci_ewb | 1500-1505 | reference article, Italian biographical dictionary, encyclopedia biography] After Spain did not welcome his proposals he went into Portuguese service at the end of 1500 (Britannica); the DBI reads the move as a consequence of what he had learned on the 1499 voyage, which suited Portugal's wish to establish what Cabral's land was, and says he was summoned to the Spanish court in 1505 on questions of navigation. These are interpretations of motive, not documented statements of it. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 60 / 0.44 to 56 / 0.40 because the motive is the biographers' inference.
      opportunity_sensing: [56, 0.4, "i", "A"],
      // [src_vespucci_dbi, src_vespucci_mariners, src_vespucci_britannica | 1496-1502 | Italian biographical dictionary, museum page, reference article] At forty-two, after the outfitting firm's collapse (its first four ships wrecked off the Spanish coast), he joined an ocean expedition in 1499 and sailed again from Lisbon in 1501; the DBI notes he got no profit from the Portuguese service and never commanded ships. The voyages were hazardous and documented, but no source shows how he weighed the risk. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 62 / 0.46 to 58 / 0.42 because exposure to risk is documented while his attitude to it is inferred.
      risk_tolerance: [58, 0.42, "i", "D"],
      // [src_vespucci_dbi, src_vespucci_ewb, src_vespucci_omodeo | 1492-1511 | Italian biographical dictionary, encyclopedia biography, partisan scholarly chapter] The DBI documents his role as factor in Berardi's partnership in Seville, his long friendship with the Florentine merchant Piero Rondinelli (named executor of his 1511 will with Manuel Cataño) and the Florentine merchant communities in Seville and Lisbon through which his letters circulated; Columbus's 1505 letter to his son, quoted in the encyclopedia biography and by Omodeo, calls him a man of good will who always wished to please him. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 60 / 0.46 to 56 / 0.40 because the Columbus remark is one quotation reported twice and the partnership is a commercial fact, not a description of working style.
      collaboration: [56, 0.4, "i", "A"],
