      source: "Engraved portrait of Juan Luna, 'Don Juan Luna y Novicio, autor de Spoliarium', on the cover of La Ilustracion Artistica (Barcelona, Montaner y Simon), issue no. 147, 20 October 1884; engraver Saderns working from a photograph (photographer not named), as catalogued by Sierra de la Calle (Archivo Agustiniano 2013, entry no. 0010). Digitised in the Biblioteca Nacional de Espana, Hemeroteca Digital, and shown as a crop on Wikimedia Commons (1019 x 1330); this copy is the Commons crop downscaled to 766 x 1000, never upscaled. The printed caption is not visible in the crop; the sitter is identified by the holder-described cover, the 1884 issue that celebrates the Spoliarium gold medal, and the scholarly catalogue entry. The BNE item viewer sits behind a security check and could not be opened, so the item-level record was not read.",
      license: "Public domain: engraving published in Spain in 1884 (before 1931, so out of copyright in the United States), by an engraver of unrecorded dates; the Biblioteca Nacional de Espana's reproduction rules (read, 28 October 2020) say public use of public-domain images from its Digital Periodical and Newspaper Library is free, under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 or equivalent licence, with the credit 'Image taken from the holdings of the Biblioteca Nacional de Espana'",
