      source: "Photograph of Kazi Nazrul Islam, standing with folded arms, printed with the Bengali caption 'kabi kaji nazrul' (Poet Kazi Nazrul) beside the poem 'Kono ek kabir prati' (To a certain poet), which honours the poet's hunger strike in prison, in Basanti (Calcutta illustrated weekly), vol. 1, part 4, issue no. 47, 1923 (printed page 263; the weekly's issue no. 42 is dated 19 May 1923). Taken from the Internet Archive scan of the University of Calcutta's copy in the Digital Library of India collection (item dli.calcutta.00534, 913 x 1193 page image); this file is the photograph cropped from that page at the scan's own resolution, not resized and not upscaled. Photographer not named. The sitter is identified by the printed caption and the poem's content. Commons holds a separate crop of the same issue's cover portrait (Basanti, 19 May 1923, signed in facsimile); that image was not used.",
