      aesthetic_sensitivity: [62, 0.46, "i", "A"],
      // [src_hikmet_salem, src_hikmet_gale, src_hikmet_britannica | 1920s-1950s | scholarly biography, reference entries] He rejected inherited Ottoman verse forms for a style of his own, and in exile wrote a play that took issue with the Stalin-era personality cult, although the same biography says he continued to uphold Soviet positions on international security and calls him not a literary conformist. The record is mixed and the independence is more clearly literary than political.
      independent_thinking: [68, 0.52, "s", "A"],
      // [src_hikmet_salem, src_hikmet_ktb, src_hikmet_hurriyet | 1928-1960 | scholarly biography, state biography, newspaper summary] He wrote poetry, plays, novels, essays and letters and earned a living as a journalist, film scriptwriter, translator and proofreader. All of it lies within writing, so this is range across literary forms rather than across unrelated fields.
      cross_domain_range: [60, 0.48, "i", "A"],
      // [src_hikmet_salem, src_hikmet_ktb, src_hikmet_hurriyet | 1930s-1950s | scholarly biography, state biography, newspaper summary] When his publishing was restricted he took work as proofreader, translator and scriptwriter, wrote columns under a pseudonym, turned to historical subjects such as the 1936 epic when contemporary topics were closed to him, and published poems under other names in the 1940s. Three accounts describe these shifts independently, though none quantifies them.
      adaptability: [64, 0.52, "s", "A"],
