      resourcefulness: [66, 0.52, "s", "A"],
      // [src_hikmet_hurriyet, src_hikmet_sabah, src_hikmet_salem, src_hikmet_ktb | 1924-1951 | newspaper summary, newspaper feature, scholarly biography, state biography] Four accounts describe repeated returns to Turkey and publication after convictions, a 1928 attempt to cross the border illegally that ended in detention, hunger strikes during imprisonment (seventeen days in 1949 after a heart attack, per the Salem biography) and the 1951 flight in a small boat. The behavior is documented in several sources, but the details vary and it was driven by overlapping political circumstances.
