      // [src_hikmet_hurriyet, src_hikmet_salem, src_hikmet_ktb | 1931-1950 | newspaper summary, scholarly biography, state biography] He faced repeated trials and convictions without recanting, is quoted in a 1931 trial affirming that he was a communist poet, went on hunger strike while imprisoned, and in exile wrote against Stalin-era dogmatism. The trial quotation comes from one newspaper summary, and the sources disagree on charges and outcomes.
      conflict_tolerance: [68, 0.52, "s", "D"],
