      creative_originality: [66, 0.48, "s", "A"],
      // [src_qian_britannica, src_qian_galcit, src_qian_lv, src_qian_archives | 1936-1956 | reference biography, department history, institutional biography, archive blog] He left MIT for Caltech in 1936 because MIT's practical focus did not suit him, joined the rocketry group's experiments, drafted with two colleagues the 1943 document that named the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, and in 1955 wrote a letter to a senior Chinese figure during the Sino-American talks asking for help to return; Britannica and the biography agree on the Caltech move, the Caltech page alone gives the 1943 document, and the biography alone describes the 1955 letter. The motives come mainly from his own later recollections and the biographers' reading.
      proactive_agency: [68, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_qian_lv, src_qian_galcit, src_qian_britannica | 1936-1956 | institutional biography, department history, reference biography] He moved from MIT to Caltech, to MIT and back to Caltech, shifted his research from aerodynamics to cybernetics, physical mechanics and games under restriction, and after 1956 changed from professor to director of a defence research academy; Britannica notes his difficulty adjusting to American culture. The shifts are documented but the sources say little about how he handled them.
      adaptability: [64, 0.46, "i", "A"],
