      // [src_rh_rhoads, src_rh_ebsco, src_rh_memoir | 1855-1902 | scholarly history, reference biography, memoir] Back in China in 1855 without a Confucian education he could not enter the civil service and refused missionary or comprador work; he became an independent tea trader and translator in Shanghai (Rhoads, reference biography), later joined Zeng Guofan's staff as a foreign-affairs expert, and after 1898 moved from Beijing to Shanghai to Hong Kong and back to the United States in 1902 (reference biography, memoir). Several career and place changes are documented, though the reasons are partly his own account. CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 64 / 0.52 to 62 / 0.5. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered to 60 / 0.5 because forced exile is not the same as chosen adaptation.
      adaptability: [60, 0.5, "s", "A"],
